#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - OHOS clang does not predefine
# _POSIX_C_SOURCE: upstream conditional-compilation branches that test
# `_POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 200112L` take the wrong (#else fallback) path and
# collide with unistd.h declarations
# Source package: cheat/1.0.4 (tests/jammed.c, tests/slow.c)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-cheat-1.0.4-posix-c-source-branch-select
trigger_tool:           clang|cc|make|conan
phase:                  build
error_signature:        static declaration of 'sleep' follows non-static declaration|static declaration of '[A-Za-z_]+' follows non-static declaration|_POSIX_C_SOURCE.*branch

severity:               2
category:               platform-libc|feature-macros|conditionals|legacy-c
match_keywords:         _POSIX_C_SOURCE, POSIX, feature-test macro, conditional compilation, unistd.h, static declaration, sleep, clang, OHOS, musl, glibc features.h, #elif
title:                  OHOS clang does not predefine _POSIX_C_SOURCE, so upstream #elif branches selecting the POSIX API take the fallback branch and clash with unistd.h; declare the POSIX level at compile time

root_cause:             Many legacy C projects guard POSIX-only code with
                        `#elif _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 200112L` and provide a
                        static fallback in `#else` (e.g. a private static
                        `sleep()`). On glibc hosts features.h implicitly
                        predefines _POSIX_C_SOURCE, so the POSIX branch is
                        taken. OHOS's clang + musl-based libc does NOT
                        predefine it by default, so the compiler takes the
                        `#else` branch and defines the private symbol —
                        which then collides with the real declaration
                        already pulled in by the same TU (e.g. cheat.h
                        enables CHEAT_POSIXLY and includes unistd.h):
                        `static declaration of 'sleep' follows non-static
                        declaration` is a hard clang error. Measured on
                        cheat 1.0.4: `tests/jammed.c:22` and
                        `tests/slow.c:20` with the OHOS clang 15 toolchain
                        (aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos).
affected_scope:         Any C/C++ project whose source or test files branch
                        on _POSIX_C_SOURCE (or siblings _XOPEN_SOURCE /
                        _GNU_SOURCE) and provide fallback definitions,
                        when compiled on OHOS; most often hits when the
                        recipe build() compiles upstream tests directly.

verification_cmd:       printf '#if _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 200112L\n#include <unistd.h>\n#else\nstatic void sleep(int s){}\n#endif\nint main(void){return 0;}' > /tmp/probe.c; /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I . -c /tmp/probe.c 2>&1 | grep -q "static declaration of 'sleep'" && /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200112L -I . -c /tmp/probe.c && echo PROBE_OK

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           declare-posix-level-cflag
rec_description:        Add `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200112L` to the compile
                        flags of the affected build (recipe build()
                        upstream-test gate, CFLAGS, or CMake
                        CMAKE_C_FLAGS). This mirrors what glibc's
                        features.h implicitly provides, so the upstream
                        `#elif _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 200112L` branch is
                        selected and the fallback static definition is
                        never compiled — no source edit, no semantic
                        change to any test.
rec_command:            clang -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200112L -I . -o prog -w tests/jammed.c && ./prog -s
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               build-option

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      rename-private-symbol
fallback_description:   If the fallback definition is truly needed
                        (non-POSIX-only builds), rename the private
                        symbol out of the libc namespace instead of
                        defining a same-name static function.
fallback_command:       sed -i 's/\bsleep(/cheat_private_sleep(/g' tests/jammed.c tests/slow.c
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          patch

forbid_1_pattern:       -Wno-error=.*static|no-error.*declaration
forbid_1_reason:        "static declaration follows non-static" is a clang
                        hard error (semantic declaration conflict), not a
                        warning; no -Wno-error flag can downgrade it.
forbid_1_consequence:   Compilation still fails at the same TU; time spent
                        chasing a non-existent flag.

forbid_2_pattern:       #define sleep|define\s+sleep\(
forbid_2_reason:        Macro-izing the symbol cannot reconcile a static
                        definition with the real unistd.h declaration; it
                        either still conflicts or corrupts the libc
                        declaration for every including TU.
forbid_2_consequence:   Compile errors move unpredictably or the libc API
                        is silently altered repo-wide.

principles:             P-BUILD-002, P-PATCH-002
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             [E032, E033, E152, DRAFT-musl-posix-decl-conflict-rename-legacy]
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-cheat-1.0.4-posix-c-source-branch-select.md
last_updated:           2026-09-19
source_event:           cheat/1.0.4 adaptation: jammed.c/slow.c compile
                        failure fixed with -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200112L in
                        the recipe build() upstream-test gate; 25/25 test
                        files then compiled and ran, conan-verify G2 PASS.
authors:                junshi_liu
source_pr:
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.85
metrics_last_used:      2026-09-19

draft:                  true
contributor_id:         junshi_liu
